00:53:17.260 --> 00:53:20.019
I know, it's nice, you're in it, you're part of it.
我知道，这很好，你在里面，你是其中的一部分。

00:53:20.019 --> 00:53:30.139
My name is Jessica, I'm a fellow Hollywood writer who, like so many of your viewers, has remained such a fan of this show because of how beautifully it treats the concept of a chosen family.
我叫杰西卡，我也是个好莱坞编剧，和你们的许多观众一样，我一直是这部剧的超级粉丝，因为这部剧对“选择的家庭”这一概念的处理是如此优美。

00:53:30.139 --> 00:53:33.980
Like Ted and Marshall, I met my best friend, Hannah, in our dorm room.
就像特德和马歇尔一样，我在宿舍里遇到了我最好的朋友汉娜。

00:53:33.980 --> 00:53:41.219
It was the fall of 2005, coincidentally, the same year, him, him premiered, and less than a year later, I met the man I would eventually marry.
那是2005年秋天，巧合的是，这也是《老妈》首播的同一年，不到一年后，我遇到了我最终要嫁的那个男人。

00:53:41.219 --> 00:53:43.460
Funnily enough, his name is Robin.
说来也巧，他的名字叫罗宾。

00:53:45.099 --> 00:53:52.099
Shortly after we finished college, Hannah reconnected with a childhood friend of hers named Christa, and the three of us immediately formed a bond.
我们大学毕业后不久，汉娜和她童年的一位朋友克里斯塔重新取得了联系，我们三个人立刻建立起了紧密的羁绊。

00:53:52.099 --> 00:53:56.139
All of us were only children, and we grew to form a sisterhood.
我们都是独生女，我们渐渐形成了一种姐妹情谊。

00:53:56.139 --> 00:54:06.820
Early on, I introduced them to himium, and it quickly became a reason for us to frequently get together, have dinner, ask philosophical questions such as, is this man a rabbit or a duck?
早期，我向她们安利了《老妈》，它很快成了我们经常聚在一起、吃晚饭、问出一些哲学问题的理由，比如，这个男人是兔子还是鸭子？

00:54:06.820 --> 00:54:19.280
And who would woo, and even set up a March Madness bracket a friend when she started using gating apps, a failed experiment, since the very first guy on the list was the guy she married.
谁会去追求？甚至当一个朋友开始使用约会软件时，还为她建立了一个疯狂三月对阵表，一个失败的实验，因为列表上的第一个男人就是她嫁的那个男人。

00:54:19.280 --> 00:54:26.723
We were inseparable for the precious years we all lived near each other in Denver, but in 2014 I took a big leap and moved to L.A.
在我们都住在丹佛附近的宝贵岁月里，我们形影不离，但在2014年，我迈出了一大步，搬到了洛杉矶，以进一步追求我的娱乐行业职业生涯。

00:54:26.723 --> 00:54:29.300
to further pursue my career in entertainment.
就像特德一样，我有一个计划，努力工作几年，建立好人脉，充实简历，然后搬回家买下完美的房子，再次和我的朋友们住得很近。

00:54:29.300 --> 00:54:37.940
Much like Ted, I had a plan, work hard for a few years, make good connections, build up that resume, then move back home to buy the perfect house and live near my friends again.
但正如特德多次学到的那样，宇宙并不是按我们的计划运转的。

00:54:37.940 --> 00:54:41.820
as Ted learned many times the universe doesn't work according to our plans.
我在洛杉矶从事独立电影工作，并磨练我作为电视编剧的手艺，长达11年，历经几次巨大成功的浪潮和更多失败的时刻。

00:54:41.820 --> 00:54:50.519
I stayed in LA working in an independent film and honing my craft as a TV writer for 11 years, writing the waves of several big moments of success and many more moments of failure.
在此期间，我们中有两人结婚了，一人有了两个可爱的孩子，正如特德的孩子们称呼他的朋友那样，他们叫我杰西阿姨。

00:54:50.519 --> 00:54:58.820
In the meantime, two of us got married and one had two wonderful children who, as Ted's children refer to his friends, call me Aunt Jesse.
作为独生子女，这是一个我从未期望听到的称呼。

00:54:58.820 --> 00:55:02.699
As an only child, it's a title I had never expected to hear.
经历了这一切，《老妈》一直是一个持久的存在，从互相发短信庆祝“快乐鞭打节”，或者在每个4月20日互相发送马歇尔吃三明治的表情包。

00:55:02.699 --> 00:55:11.595
Through it all, him-yam was a constant presence from texting each other happy-slapsgiving or sending each other gifts of Marshall eating a sandwich every 420.
毕竟我们来自科罗拉多州。

00:55:11.595 --> 00:55:18.519
We are from Colorado, after all, to watching a hungover on the couch together the morning after my husband's 40th birthday.
再到在我丈夫40岁生日的第二天早上，宿醉着一起窝在沙发上观看。

00:55:18.519 --> 00:55:22.029
Unlike Lily and Marshall, our marriage didn't ultimately make it.
不同于莉莉和马歇尔，我们的婚姻最终没能维持下去。

00:55:22.029 --> 00:55:28.400
And as I told the girls, the moment I knew we had to throw in the towel, I actually heard the sound of glass breaking.
正如我对女孩们所说的那样，在我知道我们不得不认输的那一刻，我真的听到了玻璃碎裂的声音。

00:55:28.400 --> 00:55:32.239
In 2025, the industry collapsed, had me wondering what else was out there.
在2025年，行业崩溃了，这让我开始琢磨外面还有什么。

00:55:32.239 --> 00:55:37.324
I learned that a university in England was offering a master's degree in magic and occult science.
我得知英国的一所大学正在提供魔法和神秘科学的硕士学位。

00:55:37.324 --> 00:55:38.518
And I knew I had to go.
我知道我必须去。

00:55:38.518 --> 00:55:41.890
When I told my niece, I was basically going to grown up Hogwarts.
当我告诉我的侄女，我基本上是要去成年人的霍格沃茨时。

00:55:41.890 --> 00:55:46.353
She was thrilled, but astutely asked, won't that make it harder for you to come visit?
她很兴奋，但也精明地问：那不是会让你更难来看我吗？

00:55:46.353 --> 00:55:55.485
It's been an amazing ride out here in England and I intend to stay in London for the foreseeable future, though it is indeed difficult to be farther away from my chosen family.
我在英国的这段经历简直棒极了，我打算在可预见的未来留在伦敦，尽管离我选择的家庭更远确实很不容易。

00:55:55.485 --> 00:55:58.598
What a blessing it has been to have discovered this podcast.
能发现这个播客，真的是一种福气。

00:55:58.598 --> 00:56:07.159
Now we're all rewatching the show for the five thousandth time rehashing our favorite episodes and learning more about the BTS stories that made the show so special.
现在我们都在第五千次重温这部剧，重温我们最喜欢的剧集，并更多地了解让这部剧如此特别的幕后故事。

00:56:07.159 --> 00:56:11.239
As a fellow writer and producer, I admit, that's my favorite part.
作为同行的编剧和制片人，我承认，这是我最喜欢的部分。

00:56:11.239 --> 00:56:18.239
On that note, I'm extremely grateful to Craig and Carter for not caving to the network when they tried to make you ditch the serialized nature of the storylines.
顺便说一句，我非常感谢克雷格和卡特，感谢他们在电视网试图让你们放弃剧情连载性质时没有向他们妥协。

00:56:18.239 --> 00:56:21.239
The first episode I ever watched was drumroll, please.
我看的第一集是，请敲鼓。

00:56:21.239 --> 00:56:30.800
And even though I hadn't seen the previous episode about the wedding invitation and didn't know these characters, it was the unusual storytelling and their sibling-like banter that got me on the hook.
尽管我之前没看过关于婚礼请贴的那集，也不认识这些角色，但正是这种独特的叙事方式和他们兄妹般的逗趣互怼，让我彻底入坑了。

00:56:30.800 --> 00:56:35.360
Thank you for trusting your gut and writing the show you wanted to write.
感谢你坚持内心，写出了你想创作的节目。

00:56:35.360 --> 00:56:39.920
authenticity is what made your viewers feel so connected to this fun and beautiful world.
正是这种真实感，让观众对这个有趣而美好的世界产生了强烈的共鸣。

00:56:39.920 --> 00:56:45.671
I don't know what will be in store for me while living in London, but there are two things I know for sure.
我不知道在伦敦生活期间会有什么在等着我，但我有两件事是确定的。

00:56:45.671 --> 00:56:48.734
I'll always have my sisters, and it's going to be legend.
我永远都有我的姐妹们，而且这将会是传奇般的。

00:56:48.734 --> 00:56:50.239
Wait for it, Derry, Jessica.
拭目以待吧，德里、杰西卡。

00:56:51.760 --> 00:56:52.437
That's great.
太棒了。

00:56:52.437 --> 00:57:02.185
I love that there's something magic about this letter coming because we're just talking about Harry Potter and Hogwarts and Derry Potter and Derry on Allie and like the magic of New York.
我很喜欢这封信的到来带有一种魔力，因为我们刚才还在聊哈利·波特、霍格沃茨、“德里·波特”、艾莉的德里，还有纽约的魔力。

00:57:02.185 --> 00:57:09.639
It makes me want to hear more from like fans in London of like, like, what are those weird little, like, mythological and other fans in London?
这让我想听听更多伦敦粉丝的想法，比如，那些奇怪的、小小的、带点神话色彩的伦敦粉丝都在想什么？

00:57:09.639 --> 00:57:11.840
I'm going to be doing a play in London this summer.
今年夏天我将在伦敦出演一部话剧。

00:57:11.840 --> 00:57:12.679
Fuck yeah.
太棒了。

00:57:12.679 --> 00:57:15.639
It's called Hit Machine at the Soho Theater.
它叫《命中注定》（Hit Machine），在苏荷剧院上演。

00:57:16.800 --> 00:57:20.159
Basically, it's July through like mid-August.
基本上是从7月一直演到8月中旬左右。

00:57:20.159 --> 00:57:24.000
Check it out, it's a great play by John Karen, Ben Harper's doing the music.
大家去看看吧，这是约翰·卡伦（John Karen）写的一部非常棒的话剧，音乐是本·哈珀（Ben Harper）做的。

00:57:24.000 --> 00:57:28.480
It's a really cool, so bringing the fam over to London this summer, I'm really excited about it.
真的很酷，所以今年夏天我要把家人带到伦敦去，我对此感到非常兴奋。

00:57:28.480 --> 00:57:32.760
And maybe I'll meet some people who are into the magic and occult sciences.
也许我会遇到一些对魔法和神秘学感兴趣的人。

00:57:32.760 --> 00:57:34.719
Go see it, go see the show, Jessica.
去看看吧，去看这场演出，杰西卡。

00:57:34.719 --> 00:57:36.519
You're part of the pod now.
你现在也是播客的一员了。

00:57:36.519 --> 00:57:40.440
We've read your letter, you go support Josh, come say hi.
我们读了你的信，你得去支持乔什，去跟他说个嗨。

00:57:40.440 --> 00:57:41.480
That was an awesome letter.
那是一封太棒的信。

00:57:41.480 --> 00:57:45.039
Thank you for, I love how that letter covered this like epic scope of her life.
谢谢你，我特别喜欢那封信展现了她人生的宏大格局。

00:57:45.039 --> 00:57:49.079
Like just shared this huge kind of portrait of very hymium style.
就像是以“老爸老妈浪漫史”的风格，分享了这样一幅宏大的画卷。

00:57:49.079 --> 00:57:55.800
Like here's what my life has been ending in this completely unexpected new chapter that is so adventurous and weird.
这就是我的人生经历，而现在它迎来了这样一个充满冒险又古怪的、完全意想不到的新篇章。

00:57:55.800 --> 00:58:00.159
I'm sure Jessica herself couldn't have predicted that that's where it was all leading to.
我相信杰西卡自己也绝对预测不到事情会发展到这一步。

00:58:00.159 --> 00:58:01.000
It's great.
这太棒了。

00:58:01.000 --> 00:58:02.159
So update us.
所以随时给我们更新情况。

00:58:02.159 --> 00:58:05.559
and let us know how the magic of it all works out.
让我们知道这一切的魔力是如何发挥作用的。

00:58:05.559 --> 00:58:06.400
That's a great story.
真是个精彩的故事。

00:58:06.400 --> 00:58:08.219
Thanks for sharing it.
谢谢你分享它。

00:58:08.219 --> 00:58:10.639
I am guilty.
我有罪。

00:58:10.639 --> 00:58:12.519
Please equip me.
请给我装备吧。

00:58:12.519 --> 00:58:17.309
All sins are forgiven in New York City.
在纽约市，所有的罪过都可以被原谅。

